        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-15T21:23:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CONFIG is intended to add x86_non_dsx_adlp_nonpwrseq_sm.c which contains power sequence signal handlers for platforms where external power sequencer chips are not present, this way EC takes care of ADC signals monitoring. To me GPIO_CONTROL seems too generic. Maybe we could separate this implementation in two CONFIG\u0027s one for GPIO_CONTROL and other for ADC monitoring?",
      "parentUuid": "17029db3_8016d6fb",
      "revId": "9940b2245de6672a5f49bd108f036d43c8099301",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "479caa25_1da9bf23",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/nissa/prj_nivviks.conf",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T01:20:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That could work. To me, a config item should be more about what it does, rather than what it doesn\u0027t do (or have), hence the suggestion of\nCONFIG_X86_NON_DSX_ADL_GPIO_CONTROL rather than CONFIG_X86_NON_DSX_ADL_NO_EXT_PS_CHIP, which seems unwieldy and perhaps not\nas descriptive as it should be.\nHaving a separate item for ADC monitoring may be the right thing.\nConfig items can proliferate, so it\u0027s always a tricky balance.\nSetting appropriate defaults and dependencies is important, so that folks can have a working minimal default, but can override it for corner cases without having to play the game of figuring out a large number of configs (and how they interact).",
      "parentUuid": "ccfe17d3_91d3d5e5",
      "revId": "9940b2245de6672a5f49bd108f036d43c8099301",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
